{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusQDifference","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusQDifference","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.twistedComm_eq_zero_iff_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.twistedComm_eq_zero_iff_const","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusQDifference.lean#L156-L164","doc":"**Zero q-derivative means constant, algebraically.** In the quantum torus over `R[M^±]`\nwith `σ(M) = u·M`, an element of the coefficient ring commutes with `L` iff it is a constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma_eq_self_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma_eq_self_iff","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusQDifference.lean#L131-L154","doc":"**The `σ`-invariants of `R[M^±]` are the constants** (`R` a domain, `u` not a root of\nunity). This is \"q-difference zero ⇒ constant\", proved by comparing coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma_scaleAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.sigma_scaleAction","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusQDifference.lean#L125-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.scaleAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.scaleAction","